  "notes": "{犯|おか}す means to commit a crime, offense, or mistake. It always carries a negative connotation — the object is something wrong or undesirable.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: Xを{犯|おか}す\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {罪|つみ}を{犯|おか}す: to commit a crime/sin\n- {法|ほう}を{犯|おか}す: to break the law\n- {過|あやま}ちを{犯|おか}す: to make an error\n- ミスを{犯|おか}す: to make a mistake\n\nHOMOPHONES (IMPORTANT):\nThree verbs are read おかす with different kanji and meanings:\n- {犯|おか}す: to commit (a crime) — this entry\n- {侵|おか}す: to invade, to violate (rights, territory)\n- {冒|おか}す: to brave, to risk ({危険|きけん}を{冒|おか}す)",
